{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the chirping of birds, a sound he usually found pleasant. Today, however, it felt…programmed. The sunlight seemed too bright, the colors too saturated. He sat up in bed, the floral pattern on his duvet unnervingly detailed. A notification popped into his vision – a translucent box hovering above his head: \"Quest Available: Gather 5 Wild Berries.\" He blinked, convinced he was dreaming, but the box remained. He looked around his room, noticing the perfect symmetry of the furniture, the almost comical placement of knick-knacks. His reflection in the mirror wasn't quite right; his eyes were too wide, his jawline too sharp. A creeping sense of dread began to coil in his stomach. This wasn’t his life.\n\n***\n\nHe cautiously opened his bedroom door and stepped into the world. The street was eerily clean, the houses uniformly charming. People strolled by with vacant smiles, occasionally pausing to read text that appeared above their heads – dialogue boxes. He saw a woman with a \"Vendor\" label floating beside her, offering \"Healing Potion\" for 50 gold. Arthur instinctively reached for his wallet, realizing he had none. He tried to speak, to ask someone what was happening, but his voice came out as a pre-recorded phrase: \"Greetings, traveler! Are you in need of assistance?\" Panic seized him. He was trapped, a character in someone else's game, forced to follow a pre-determined path, collect berries, and apparently, engage in bland, scripted conversations. His only hope was to somehow break free from this digital prison.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -1.3997840881347656}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.05491254851222038}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.00344469235278666}, {"token": "▁chir", "logprob": -0.1953982263803482}, {"token": "ping", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁o